-- 050: mosaic_capacity_pbi_metric_view re-created with business metadata (GENERATED by _enrich_metric_view_metadata.py from the
-- live definition + metric_view_metadata/mosaic_capacity_pbi_metric_view.json). Logic identical to live (asserted). edw_test only.
CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW edw_test.enterprise_analytics.mosaic_capacity_pbi_metric_view
COMMENT 'MOSAIC CAPACITY - executive capacity and utilization view, PowerBI ''Mosaic Impact Report'' parity (draft, edw_test only). One row per radiologist shift; measures are per-shift averages in TBWU 26 exactly as the PowerBI Practice Summary page: baseline vs new capacity, added capacity, utilization (reading time / shift time), efficiency and Mosaic share. PowerBI defaults are already applied: only shifts with a baseline, the report''s shift-length filter (about 4-16 hours) and the PowerBI ''All Shifts'' window. Filter groups to Has TBWU26 Baseline = 1 to match PowerBI tables and totals. This is THE view for exec capacity / added capacity / utilization questions; mosaic_capacity_metric_view is the detailed case-mix companion.'
WITH METRICS
LANGUAGE YAML
AS
$$
version: 1.1
source: edw_test.enterprise_analytics.mosaic_capacity_pbi_shift_vw
filter: in_pbi_default
comment: 'MOSAIC CAPACITY - executive capacity and utilization view, PowerBI ''Mosaic Impact Report'' parity (draft, edw_test
  only). One row per radiologist shift; measures are per-shift averages in TBWU 26 exactly as the PowerBI Practice Summary
  page: baseline vs new capacity, added capacity, utilization (reading time / shift time), efficiency and Mosaic share. PowerBI
  defaults are already applied: only shifts with a baseline, the report''s shift-length filter (about 4-16 hours) and the
  PowerBI ''All Shifts'' window. Filter groups to Has TBWU26 Baseline = 1 to match PowerBI tables and totals. This is THE
  view for exec capacity / added capacity / utilization questions; mosaic_capacity_metric_view is the detailed case-mix companion.'
dimensions:
- name: Shift Date
  expr: source.ShiftDate
  comment: Date of the radiologist's shift (e.g. 2026-09-15). Bind dashboard Period / date-range filters here.
  display_name: Shift Date
  synonyms:
  - date of shift
  - shift day
  - date worked
- name: Month
  expr: source.shift_month
  comment: Calendar month of the shift, as the first day of the month (e.g. 2026-09-01) - the PowerBI Month slicer. Use for
    monthly trends; the current month is partial.
  display_name: Month
  synonyms:
  - shift month
  - reporting month
  - calendar month
- name: Local Region
  expr: source.local_region
  comment: One of 6 fixed regions - Special Operations, Apex, Genesis, Maverick, Trailblazer, Matrix - or 'Blank' for unmapped
    teams. Exact copy of PowerBI '0. Cur'[Local], keyed on Team. Filter with equality (= 'Apex'), not LIKE.
  display_name: Local Region
  synonyms:
  - region
  - local
  - operating region
- name: Area
  expr: source.area
  comment: Geographic area keyed on Team, exact copy of PowerBI '0. Cur'[Area]. Values such as East, Great Lakes, Midwest,
    Northeast, Southwest, West, Envision, Integration & SEAL, VRad, Matrix, or 'Blank'.
  display_name: Area
  synonyms:
  - geographic area
  - PowerBI area
  - area grouping
- name: Team
  expr: source.Team
  comment: Radiologist's roster team, a sub-team finer than Team Rolled Up (Provider Practice), e.g. 'RAF Tampa', 'SVDI San
    Ramon'. For the radiologist's home practice use Team Rolled Up.
  display_name: Team
  synonyms:
  - sub team
  - roster team
  - radiologist team
- name: Team Rolled Up
  expr: source.team_rolled_up
  comment: Provider Practice = the radiologist's home practice (PowerBI 'Team Rolled up', Team mapped through the team_rollups
    lookup). Default for 'by practice / group' questions unless the user means the site or managing practice (Local Practice).
  display_name: Provider Practice (Team Rolled Up)
  synonyms:
  - provider practice
  - home practice
  - rolled up team
  - group
- name: Local Practice
  expr: source.localpractice
  comment: Practice the shift is reported under in the PowerBI Practice Summary table rows (PowerBI '0. Cur'[localpractice],
    shown as 'Practice'); treated as Managing / site Practice. Not the radiologist's home practice - that is Team Rolled Up.
  display_name: Practice (Managing Practice)
  synonyms:
  - managing practice
  - practice
  - site practice
  - PowerBI practice
- name: Radiologist
  expr: source.Rad_name
  comment: Radiologist name, 'Last, First M' (e.g. 'Taha, Manuel R'). Match partial names with ILIKE '%name%'.
  display_name: Radiologist
  synonyms:
  - radiologist name
  - rad
  - doctor
  - physician
- name: NPI
  expr: CAST(source.NPI AS STRING)
  comment: Radiologist's National Provider Identifier (10-digit ID, text). Use to identify a radiologist unambiguously.
  display_name: Radiologist NPI
  synonyms:
  - NPI number
  - provider ID
  - national provider identifier
- name: Baseline Type
  expr: source.Baseline_type
  comment: 'How the shift''s baseline was set: Exact, Proxy, Manual Review, etc. The view already keeps only shifts with a
    baseline (PowerBI default) - do not filter this for exec numbers.'
  display_name: Baseline Type
  synonyms:
  - baseline method
  - baseline source
  - how baseline was set
- name: Model
  expr: source.model
  comment: PowerBI 'Model' slicer value (source column Model_type) attached to the shift's radiologist record.
  display_name: Model
  synonyms:
  - model type
  - PowerBI model
- name: Data Quality
  expr: source.Shift_Data_Quality_Status
  comment: Shift data quality status from the source. The PowerBI Time Series page filters to 'Good'; the Practice Summary
    defaults used here do not.
  display_name: Shift Data Quality
  synonyms:
  - data quality status
  - shift quality flag
  - good data shifts
- name: Shift Length (hours)
  expr: source.shift_length_rounded
  comment: Shift length rounded to whole hours (PowerBI Shift Length Display), e.g. 8, 10, 12. Only the PowerBI report's allowed
    lengths (about 4-16 hours) are in this view.
  display_name: Shift Length (Hours)
  synonyms:
  - shift length
  - shift hours
  - hours per shift
measures:
- name: Selected Shift Count
  expr: COUNT(1)
  comment: Number of shifts in scope after the PowerBI Practice Summary defaults (shifts with a baseline, allowed shift lengths,
    'All Shifts' window). Slice by Month or Shift Date. = PowerBI [Selected Shift Ct.] (Mosaic Impact).
  display_name: Shifts in Scope
  synonyms:
  - shift count
  - number of shifts
  - shifts counted
  - selected shift ct
- name: Average Baseline
  expr: AVG(source.shift_baseline_RPWU)
  comment: Average pre-Mosaic baseline workload per shift, in TBWU 26 per shift (each radiologist's own baseline for that
    shift). Only shifts with a baseline count. = PowerBI [Average Baseline (Top N)] (Mosaic Impact), unit TBWU 26/Shift.
  display_name: Average Baseline per Shift (TBWU 26)
  synonyms:
  - baseline per shift
  - baseline capacity
  - pre-Mosaic capacity
  - average baseline TBWU
- name: New Capacity
  expr: AVG(source.on_shift_capacity_RPWU)
  comment: Average workload read per shift with Mosaic (on-shift capacity), in TBWU 26 per shift. Only shifts with a baseline
    count. Compare to Average Baseline. = PowerBI [New Capacity (Top N)] (Mosaic Impact), unit TBWU 26/Shift.
  display_name: New Capacity per Shift (TBWU 26)
  synonyms:
  - capacity per shift
  - capacity with Mosaic
  - Mosaic capacity per shift
  - current capacity
- name: Addl Capacity Per Shift
  expr: CASE WHEN AVG(source.shift_baseline_RPWU) IS NULL THEN NULL ELSE AVG(source.on_shift_capacity_RPWU) - AVG(source.shift_baseline_RPWU)
    END
  comment: 'Added capacity per shift: New Capacity minus Average Baseline, in TBWU 26 per shift (positive = more work per
    shift than before Mosaic). Blank when there is no baseline. PowerBI marks practices >= 0 (rounded) as ''Successful''.
    = PowerBI [Add''l Capacity / Shift (Top N)] (Mosaic Impact).'
  display_name: Additional Capacity per Shift (TBWU 26)
  synonyms:
  - added capacity per shift
  - add'l capacity per shift
  - extra TBWU per shift
  - capacity gain per shift
- name: Pct Addl Capacity
  expr: (AVG(source.on_shift_capacity_RPWU) - AVG(source.shift_baseline_RPWU)) / NULLIF(AVG(source.shift_baseline_RPWU), 0)
  comment: 'Headline added capacity: (New Capacity - Average Baseline) / Average Baseline, a fraction (0.12 = 12% more work
    per shift than baseline; can be negative). Only shifts with a baseline; keep groups with Has TBWU26 Baseline = 1 to match
    PowerBI. = PowerBI [% Add''l Capacity (Top N)] (Mosaic Impact).'
  display_name: '% Additional Capacity vs Baseline'
  synonyms:
  - added capacity
  - '% added capacity'
  - '% add''l capacity'
  - extra capacity
  - capacity lift
  - capacity increase
- name: Pct Mosaic
  expr: SUM(source.on_shift_mosaic_cases) / NULLIF(SUM(source.on_shift_cases), 0)
  comment: Share of on-shift cases read in Mosaic, a fraction 0-1 (case-weighted across shifts in scope). = PowerBI [% Mosaic(Top
    N)] (Mosaic Impact).
  display_name: '% On-Shift Cases Read in Mosaic'
  synonyms:
  - '% Mosaic'
  - share of shift cases read in Mosaic
  - Mosaic usage on shift
  - on-shift Mosaic share
- name: Pct Mosaic Drafting
  expr: SUM(source.on_shift_mosaic_drafting_cases) / NULLIF(SUM(source.on_shift_cases), 0)
  comment: Share of on-shift cases drafted in Mosaic (AI Drafting), a fraction 0-1 (case-weighted across shifts in scope).
    = PowerBI [% Mosaic drafting (Top N)] (Mosaic Impact).
  display_name: '% On-Shift Cases Drafted in Mosaic'
  synonyms:
  - '% Mosaic Drafting'
  - share of shift cases drafted
  - drafting usage on shift
  - on-shift drafting share
- name: New Efficiency
  expr: AVG(CASE WHEN source.on_shift_efficiency_RPWU <= 1 THEN source.on_shift_efficiency_RPWU END)
  comment: 'Average per-shift efficiency with Mosaic: TBWU 26 workload relative to reading time, a raw ratio (show 3 decimals,
    not a %). Shifts with efficiency above 1 are ignored, as in PowerBI. = PowerBI [New Efficiency(Top N)] (Mosaic Impact).'
  display_name: New Efficiency per Shift
  synonyms:
  - shift efficiency
  - per-shift efficiency
  - average shift efficiency
  - new efficiency ratio
- name: New Utilization
  expr: AVG(source.on_shift_utilization_RPWU_pct / 100)
  comment: 'Headline utilization: average per-shift share of scheduled shift time spent reading (reading time / shift duration),
    a fraction 0-1 (0.74 = 74%). Averaged per shift, unit TBWU 26/Shift. = PowerBI [New Utilization(Top N)] (Mosaic Impact).'
  display_name: Utilization (Reading Time / Shift Time)
  synonyms:
  - utilization
  - shift utilization
  - busy-ness
  - reading time share of shift
  - utilization rate
- name: Has TBWU26 Baseline
  expr: MAX(CASE WHEN source.has_tbwu26 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END)
  comment: 'Building block (filter flag): 1 if any shift in the group has a TBWU 26 baseline, else 0. PowerBI hides groups
    where this is 0 (e.g. Matrix): add HAVING MEASURE(`Has TBWU26 Baseline`) = 1 by Local Practice, or pre-select qualifying
    (Local Practice, Month) pairs for totals.'
  display_name: Has TBWU 26 Baseline (PowerBI Filter)
  synonyms:
  - TBWU 26 baseline available
  - baseline available flag
  - PowerBI baseline filter
- name: Radiologist Count
  expr: COUNT(DISTINCT source.NPI)
  comment: Distinct radiologists (by NPI) with at least one shift in scope. Slice by Month, region or practice.
  display_name: Radiologists With Shifts
  synonyms:
  - number of radiologists
  - rad count
  - radiologists on shift
  - headcount on shift
- name: Data Through Date
  expr: MAX(source.ShiftDate)
  comment: Latest shift date in the source - the as-of date of the capacity data. Quote it when the user asks how current
    the numbers are.
  display_name: Data Through Date
  synonyms:
  - data as of
  - latest shift date
  - capacity data freshness
$$
